Load and save the config file, as every Doom does.

Doom keeps its settings (screen size, sound volumes, key and mouse
bindings) in default.cfg, reading it at startup and writing it back at
exit. fbDOOM comes from doomgeneric, which wraps both directions in
#if ORIGCODE for embedded targets without a filesystem, and ORIGCODE is
never defined. So fbDOOM printed "saving config in ..." but neither
read nor wrote the file, every setting reset on each launch, and a
system could not ship defaults through the user's config.

Kandelo has a filesystem, so compile the loader and saver back in,
unchanged from upstream. M_SetConfigDir already creates the directory.
This restores upstream behavior and is independent of Kandelo.

Reference: chocolate-doom src/m_config.c LoadDefaultCollection and
SaveDefaultCollection at the pinned commit.

diff --git a/fbdoom/m_config.c b/fbdoom/m_config.c
